        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/river-falls/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "River Falls’ post office opened in 1891, marking the town’s first federal presence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/river-falls/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Conecuh River runs through River Falls, shaping its early lumber industry.",
